models…\" then \"gemini-9-pro\\n gemini-9-flash\\n\\n\" to stdout. HOME tmp; two runs: without and with `--net`.\nexpected: without --net: agy row (Tools) verified, \"agy login (model list)\" row status unknown detail \"offline run: not provable without `agy models`; rerun with --net\", proof \"`agy models` (network)\"; and the agy log has exactly one line `--version` (proving no network call off the flag). With --net: log has `--version` and `models`; login row status verified, detail \"3 models: gemini-9-pro, gemini-9-flash, …\" hmm — ids[:4] join then \" …\" → with 2 ids: \"2 models: gemini-9-pro, gemini-9-flash …\". Let me use 3 ids to be safe: \"3 models: a, b, c …\" with the trailing ellipsis always present. The \"Fetching…\" line must NOT be counted (filtered by `not l.lower().startswith(\"fetching\")`), blank lines skipped. And rc 0 both ways.\ncan_fail_because: flip the offline branch to run `agy models` regardless of `net`, or delete the `startswith(\"fetching\")` filter → the login count includes the banner (4 models) and the no-flag log gains a `models` line → both red.\n\nCareful: also note test must not be flaky: the fake agy `models` must return quickly (NET_TIMEOUT 30).\n\nRT-13 — `--blueprint` / `--workflows` / usage errors\nsetup: tmp cwd; blueprint dir `bp/` with README.md, a.md, b.md, notes.txt (non-.md must not count); second run points at `nope/`; a fake bin dir (all MISSING) so nothing real runs.\naction: (a) `--blueprint bp`; (b) `--blueprint nope --json`; (c) `--workflows wf` where wf/ has two .js files and one .py; (d) bad flag `--nope`; (e) `--blueprint` with no DIR; (f) `--require a b`.\nexpected: (a) Skills row \"blueprint (<abs path>)\" status verified detail \"3 sections, map present: README.md, a.md, b.md\" (notes.txt excluded) and rc 0; (b) status MISSING \"directory not found\" + rc **1** (an explicitly named blueprint is a hard fail — the blueprint loop in `exit_code`); (c) row detail \"2: a.js, b.js\" (`list_names` keeps .js/.mjs/